{
  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "items": [
        "Debezium snapshots each table first, then streams its changes \u2014 one ordered flow per table",
        "Everything lands in the same append-only Bronze layer, snapshot and CDC alike",
        "Nothing is ever edited in Bronze \u2014 corrections arrive as new change events"
      ],
      "title": "Snapshot, Then Stream"
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "items": [
        "Schema, null, uniqueness and row-count checks run before data reaches Silver",
        "Failing batches are quarantined and alerted, never silently dropped or silently promoted",
        "Gold is built only from gated Silver data"
      ],
      "title": "Quality Is a Gate, Not a Hope"
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "items": [
        "Delivery is at-least-once: Kafka and Debezium can and do redeliver",
        "Silver uses idempotent MERGE on the primary key, so a replay changes nothing",
        "The effect is exactly-once even though the delivery is not"
      ],
      "title": "Exactly-Once Effects, Honestly"
    }
  ],
